## 1. Objective restatement (acceptance surface)

Produce `reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md`: for each of 3 real sealed goals
(`B0.0`, `B0.1`, `B0.2`), a hand-extraction into the SAEOS-1 §4.3 node types recording
per-field `extractable` / `partial` / `absent`, with an explicit `GO`/`NO-GO` verdict and the
loss ratio (`backlog/SAKG-1-backlog.yaml` `S-PROBE.deliverables`).

The four acceptance predicates, **verbatim and unaltered** (`S-PROBE.accept`):

```
test -f reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md
rg -q '^verdict: (GO|NO-GO)$' reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md
test $(rg -c '^## goal: ' reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md) -ge 3
rg -q '^loss_ratio: 0\.[0-9]+$' reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md
```

This restates the backlog node without adding, relaxing, or reinterpreting any requirement.
The plan does **not** restate or revise the probe's verdict; under CER-5 the disposition of
`NO-GO` belongs to the founder at `G-S1-GO`, not to this plan.

